eq \overline{\mathcal{F}}$. Let $y$ denote the (non-special) vertex of $\overline{\mathcal{C}}$ opposite $\mathcal{F}$, and $w\in G$ a reflection in the wall of ${\mathcal{A}}$ containing $\mathcal{F}$ (viewed as a representative of the corresponding element of the affine Weyl group). Adopting the convention that a matrix ring stands for its intersection with $\mathrm{Sp}_4(F)$, we compute directly that  egin{equation} G_{\mathcal{C}} =  mat{{\scriptstyle{\mathcal{O}}} & {\scriptstyle{\mathcal{O}}} & {\scriptstyle{\mathcal{O}}} & {\scriptstyle{\mathcal{O}}} \ \mathfrak{p} & {\scriptstyle{\mathcal{O}}} & {\scriptstyle{\mathcal{O}}}&{\scriptstyle{\mathcal{O}}} \ \mathfrak{p} &\mathfrak{p} & {\scriptstyle{\mathcal{O}}}&\mathfrak{p}\ \mathfrak{p}&\mathfrak{p}&{\scriptstyle{\mathcal{O}}}&{\scriptstyle{\mathcal{O}}}} \quad 	ext{and} \quad G_{w\mathcal{C}} =  mat{{\scriptstyle{\mathcal{O}}} & \mathfrak{p} & {\scriptstyle{\mathcal{O}}} & {\scriptstyle{\mathcal{O}}} \ {\scriptstyle{\mathcal{O}}} & {\scriptstyle{\mathcal{O}}} & {\scriptstyle{\mathcal{O}}}&{\scriptstyle{\mathcal{O}}} \ \mathfrak{p} &\mathfrak{p} & {\scriptstyle{\mathcal{O}}}&{\scriptstyle{\mathcal{O}}}\ \mathfrak{p}&\mathfrak{p}&\mathfrak{p}&{\scriptstyle{\mathcal{O}}}}, \end{equation} each of which contains $T$ as a subgroup. It therefore follows that $\{y,wy\} \subset \overline{\mathcal{C}}\cup \overline{w\mathcal{C}}\subseteq {\mathcal{A}}^T$, even though neither $y$ nor $wy$ lie in $\overline{\mathcal{F}}$. Applying now Lemma~ef{L:strongunicityfails}, we deduce that strong unicity fails for any supercuspidal representation $\pi(\Psi)$ constructed from $G^0=T$.
